from lesson_writer import author,CPP

def write(name,purpose,steps,adapt,detail,exercise,limits):
 def tests(link):return detail+'\n\nEvidence: '+link(CPP/'support/ObjectOracle.java','Java oracle')+', '+link(CPP/'support/objects.cpp','native harness')+' and '+link(CPP/'tools/object_differential.py','object differential driver')+'. The inspected object report records 9,244 matching observations across the complete corpus. That total is not this file’s test count; generic ERROR normalization does not prove exact exception classes.'
 author('src/org/minima/objects/'+name+'.md',purpose,steps,adapt,tests,exercise,limits+' Counterpart status remains partial and full parity not_verified.')

write('Address','Connects a script or raw address bytes to a human-readable Mx address with an error-detecting checksum.',[
 'The script constructor wraps text in MiniString, builds a zero-sum single-leaf MMR and derives the root. That root hash becomes the address bytes. The raw-data constructor instead records empty script text and accepts the supplied address bytes.',
 'For Mx encoding, hash the raw bytes and take the first four hash bytes as checksum. Build an envelope containing sentinel byte 1, a two-byte length, the address bytes and checksum, then Base32 encode it.',
 'The nonzero sentinel prevents numeric Base32 conversion from losing the beginning of the envelope. It is structural data rather than part of the address itself.',
 'Decoding first checks that sentinel, reads a signed Java short length, reads the requested payload and four checksum bytes, and compares them with a newly calculated checksum. It does not require end-of-stream after the checksum.',
 'Equality compares only address bytes. JSON also exposes script and Mx text, but these are not additional equality conditions.',
 'Serialize hash-encoded address bytes followed by script. Reading rebuilds Mx text from the address bytes; it does not recompute the bytes from the script or validate their consistency.'
], 'The native script constructor reuses the mathematical equivalence that a one-leaf proof is empty, directly returning its leaf hash. Mx encoding reuses BaseConverter and SHA3; decoding reproduces the signed-short boundary with an explicit JavaNegativeArraySizeException when the high bit is set. Native TRUE_ADDRESS is const, unlike Java’s mutable static field.',
 'Script cases include empty, boolean and Unicode text and compare full address bytes/JSON. Seeded raw byte cases of lengths up to 64 are encoded to Mx, decoded again, and mutated in the final character to test checksum rejection. These sizes do not cover the signed-short length boundary or arbitrary trailing-envelope bytes.',
 'Why can a deserialized address retain a script that does not hash to its stored bytes? Which separate validation would be needed if a caller wanted that invariant?',
 'The checksum detects accidental changes; it does not establish ownership or signature validity. Default Java Address fields are null before reading, whereas the native default contains empty values. Exact null/default behavior and all oversized envelope cases remain open.')
write('Token','Describes a custom token’s originating coin, denomination scale, total backing amount, name, script and creation block; its identifier commits to those serialized details.',[
 'Store the constructor fields, copying the token script through MiniString, then calculate the token ID. The special IDs 0x00 and 0xFF identify Minima and token creation respectively.',
 'Scale an underlying Minima amount into token units by multiplying by ten in a loop scale.getAsInt times. Reverse conversion divides by ten in the same loop. A negative loop count performs no operations; fractional scales are narrowed to int before iteration.',
 'Total tokens uses the scaling operation on the stored backing amount. Reported decimal places are 44 minus the narrowed scale; this getter does not independently validate a sensible token denomination.',
 'Serialize coin ID with the hash limit, then script, scale, backing amount, name and created block. To derive the ID, wrap those bytes in MiniData and hash that object, including its length prefix. Hashing only the raw token bytes would give a different result.',
 'For JSON, a trimmed name beginning with { is inserted as a MiniString object rather than parsed as JSON. Other names are ordinary quoted strings. Malformed brace-prefixed text can therefore produce malformed JSON output.',
 'Reading restores all six serialized fields then recalculates the token ID. Java ID calculation catches any Exception and logs it; the convenience converter separately catches IOException and returns null.'
], 'Native members are values and token ID is optional. Native JSON explicitly emits brace-prefixed name text as raw JSON to preserve the Java object serialization behavior. It uses bit-level wraparound for decimal-place subtraction. Its ID calculation catches runtime_error and resets the optional, while Java’s catch is broader and logs; failure parity remains a review item.',
 'The token branch crosses scales -1, 0, 1, 6, 18 and 44 with ordinary names, JSON-looking names, malformed JSON-looking names and Unicode. It compares wire bytes, total/decimals JSON and the recomputed token ID. Coin fixtures also attach token metadata. No dedicated assertion here proves all possible scale narrowing or caught-error logging behavior.',
 'A backing amount of 0.001 at scale 3 represents how many token units? Why is replacing the repeated division loop with one floating-point multiplication unsafe for a parity port?',
 'The stored scale is a MiniNumber, so its textual declaration alone does not guarantee it is a valid small nonnegative integer. Validation at token-creation/consensus call sites must be studied separately.')
write('Witness','Collects the signatures, input coin proofs and script proofs supplied alongside a transaction. It stores evidence; it does not decide whether that evidence is valid.',[
 'Initialize three independent lists. Each clear method removes only its corresponding category.',
 'addSignature rejects Java null and deduplicates by the root public key’s canonical hex string. isSignedBy compares that exact string, so this is a membership query rather than cryptographic signature verification.',
 'Coin proofs are appended without deduplication. Script proofs are deduplicated by address bytes; getScript returns the first matching proof or null.',
 'The list getters expose Java’s mutable lists. Callers can therefore bypass add-method deduplication by modifying a returned collection.',
 'JSON emits signatures, mmrproofs and scripts. Binary output uses the same category order, prefixing each list with a MiniNumber count.',
 'Reading replaces each category list immediately before reading its count, then appends decoded entries directly. It does not call the deduplicating add methods. Duplicate entries on the wire are preserved, and a failed read can leave earlier categories replaced while later ones retain old contents.'
], 'Native vectors preserve category order and expose mutable getters. readDataStream deliberately clears and fills each vector in sequence to retain observable partial-read ordering. Element storage is by value; a pointer returned by getScript can be invalidated by later vector growth, unlike a Java object reference that remains alive through garbage collection.',
 'The witness fixture uses counts 0, 1, 2 and 5. Each iteration adds the same signature twice and the TRUE script twice but appends one coin proof, so matching output directly checks insertion deduplication and coin accumulation. Java-produced wire, truncated and trailing variants exercise reconstruction. This fixture does not by itself authenticate signatures or prove alias lifetime behavior.',
 'Why can reading a serialized witness produce duplicate scripts even though addScript prevents them? Which API path would a test need to use to distinguish those behaviors?',
 'A native Signature passed by value cannot express Java null. Ownership, retained references and arbitrary direct list mutation need focused tests beyond the ordinary object fixture. Consensus checking remains in TxPoWChecker and related code.')
